import Mathlib

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

/-!
# The explicit data of the `M_{50,1/25}` certificate (Polymath8a, Theorem 3.13(i))

`certBasis` lists the 1780 elements `(a, alpha)` of the `d = 25` basis
`(1 + eps - P_1)^a * P_alpha` (Polymath8a §7.1), in the same order as
`Submission/numerics/cand_k50_d25.json`.

`certCoefSym` are the coefficients of the *symmetric monomial* basis (after dividing
the raw json coefficients by their gcd `certGcd`), and `certCoefLab` the coefficients in
the *labelled* basis `(1+eps-P_1)^a * lmono alpha` (which is the symmetric basis rescaled
diagonally by `thetas alpha = prod_v (count_v alpha)!`):
`certCoefLab j = certK * certCoefSym j / thetas (alpha j)`, `certK = 12! = 479001600`.
Both vectors realise the *same* test function up to a global factor, hence have the same
Rayleigh quotient `4.001246593441841... > 4`.

The final arithmetic obligation is `50 * certqJ * certDI > 4 * certqI * certDJ`
(equivalently `certRatio > 4`), where `certqI`, `certqJ`, `certDI`, `certDJ` are the exact
integer quadratic forms / common denominators of `Submission/numerics/rq_k50_d25.json`
(with `certqI`, `certqJ` divided by `certGcd^2` to match the reduced coefficients).
-/

open scoped BigOperators

namespace Commons.NumberTheory.MaynardSieve

